The seasonal-name change has no material defect identified in this review. The new path-based move workflow has unresolved safety and correctness defects.
- {'id': 'F1', 'severity': 'high', 'path': 'tools/file_moves.py:53', 'evidence': 'The health check examines only the source and destination strings. A P path row can move an ancestor such as 00_Primary_Storage_Drive/10_ARCHIVE, carrying its Health_and_Wellness subtree with it. An index-only descendant check would also miss DexaProject because drive_index.py deliberately excludes that folder and its contents.', 'fix': 'Before moving a folder, inspect its live descendant hierarchy for protected folders, including folders omitted from the index, and refuse the move if the scan is incomplete or finds one.'}
- {'id': 'F2', 'severity': 'high', 'path': 'tools/file_moves.py:115', 'evidence': "The live check verifies only the item's immediate parent, name, trash status and sharing status. If an ancestor is moved into Health_and_Wellness or renamed after the index was built, the immediate parent remains unchanged, so a previously indexed P path row can move the item out of a protected path.", 'fix': 'Resolve and validate the live source and destination ancestry immediately before each move, refusing changed, ambiguous, inaccessible or protected paths.'}
- {'id': 'F3', 'severity': 'medium', 'path': 'tools/file_moves.py:104', 'evidence': 'The shared filing log treats every previously moved ID as permanently complete. After a project folder is moved from _ACTIVE to _STALLED, a later valid plan to move that same folder back is silently skipped, even after the index is rebuilt.', 'fix': 'Scope idempotency to the intended move, including its source parent, destination and name, and report skipped jobs explicitly.'}
- {'id': 'F4', 'severity': 'high', 'path': 'tools/file_moves.py:118', 'evidence': 'A failed destination-name lookup becomes an empty list because a failed or error-shaped gws response is replaced with {}. The code then proceeds with the move even if the destination already contains that name, defeating the required live name-taken guard.', 'fix': 'Require a successful, well-formed list response before moving; treat API errors and incomplete lookups as errors rather than as an empty destination.'}
- {'id': 'F5', 'severity': 'medium', 'path': 'tools/file_moves.py:83', 'evidence': 'A destination with multiple indexed folder matches is treated as missing rather than a problem. ensure() subsequently selects the first live match without checking uniqueness, so a P path move can land in an arbitrary same-named folder.', 'fix': 'Report ambiguous destination paths as problems and validate uniqueness at every live path component before moving.'}
- {'id': 'F6', 'severity': 'medium', 'path': 'tools/file_moves.py:90', 'evidence': 'For a destination absent from dests, ensure() recursively resolves its parent, but only complete job destinations are seeded in dests and there is no root base case. A new destination whose ancestors are not also job destinations therefore recurses through the empty path until it fails instead of creating the folder.', 'fix': 'Seed the Drive root ID and resolve each existing ancestor explicitly, with a terminating root case and failure handling.'}
LIMITS ['No tests or dry runs were executed, as requested.', 'Live Drive state and API behavior were not inspected.']
